  "adaptations": [
    "Native JUCE alternative layout with live parameter controls; no reference PNG is used as a background or screenshot.",
    "All three oscillator algorithms and parameter names come from the current patch, replacing illustrative wavetable, analogue and FM labels and made-up preset names.",
    "Each oscillator uses the reference's four-column primary-knob geometry; pitch remains a live compact semitone field in the lower tuning row. Mute and solo remain accessible alongside octave and key tracking.",
    "The concept's third standalone envelope is an explicitly labeled LFO 3 envelope bank, using Surge's real LFO 3 ADSR controls. The real amplitude and filter envelopes remain independently visible.",
    "Filter A and B denote Surge's two filter units within the selected scene, not two different scenes. Shared waveshaper drive and filter balance replace nonexistent independent per-filter drive or mix controls.",
    "The compact routing strip depicts the native routing selection rather than claiming arbitrary cable editing.",
    "Eight working macros are arranged along the bottom. The concept's pitch/mod wheels are replaced by accurately labeled scene-pitch and FM-depth faders; the full editor retains MIDI expression controls.",
    "The eight visible effect slots use live algorithm menus; all sixteen native effect slots remain available in the full editor.",
    "The header uses working preset, scene, skin and full-editor navigation. Hardware texture and beveled outlines are procedural native drawing, not a pixel-identical photograph.",
    "Native parameter, automation, scaling and screenshot validation must pass before this layout is considered verified.",
    "The master gain follows the far-right header position. Scene output remains editable through Full editor rather than occupying an invented second header master dial.",
    "Scene and voice mode controls that conflict with the reference navigation are available through Full editor; the reference scene buttons retain actual Scene A/B selection."
  ]
}
